 "summary": "Commodities were broadly weaker in the latest session, with 5 of the 24 tracked benchmarks higher and 17 lower. Energy was mixed, 1 of 4 higher, the biggest move coming from Natural Gas at +2.37% to 3.27 USD/MMBtu; precious metals were mixed, 3 of 5 higher, the biggest move coming from Gold at +0.97% to 4145.47 USD/t oz; base metals fell across the board, led by Tin at -2.71% to 51767 USD/T; bulk and battery materials were mixed, 1 of 5 higher, the biggest move coming from Rare Earth Elements at -5.84% to 39.95 USD/share; agriculture fell across the board, led by Sugar at -1.28% to 20.84 USd/Lbs. The largest single move across the complex was Rare Earth Elements at -5.84%. Tin has not refreshed past the prior day's print and is flagged accordingly, being fixed periodically rather than traded continuously. Rare earths are represented by the MP Materials equity proxy, as no reliable daily spot benchmark is published. Reported alongside the session, Business Standard on 13 October 2026:",
